(1297836, 165064, 7560, '<td valign="top">Aersome surfing shot! These shots are really hard to expose for, because you can lose detail in the shadow areas. The face is still a tad dark, but you can make it out. Very nicely done! 7</td>', 'Aersome surfing shot! These shots are really hard to expose for, because you can lose detail in the shadow areas. The face is still a tad dark, but you can make it out. Very nicely done! 7', '2005-04-17 13:24:18.000000', NULL, 1),
(1297837, 164238, 22734, '<td valign="top">This is certainly and without doubt one of those amazing images so expertly captured that the viewer needs a towel to wipe off the spray. The detail is breathtaking and it is one of those images that can do full justice to any wall. 8</td>', 'This is certainly and without doubt one of those amazing images so expertly captured that the viewer needs a towel to wipe off the spray. The detail is breathtaking and it is one of those images that can do full justice to any wall. 8', '2005-04-17 13:26:19.000000', NULL, 1),
(1297838, 164452, 7560, '<td valign="top">Hmmm, I''d work  on the grip on the hammer. ;) Jokes aside, I think a longer exposure where you see the hammer coming down would look very cool. 6</td>', 'Hmmm, I''d work  on the grip on the hammer. ;) Jokes aside, I think a longer exposure where you see the hammer coming down would look very cool. 6', '2005-04-17 13:28:40.000000', NULL, 1),
(1297842, 164868, 7560, '<td valign="top">I like the crop and the action. My biggest concern with this image would be the overall clutter in the shot. Nothing is really isolated out here. With the ump right on top of the play the motion is interrupted. See how he basically creates a vertical line that stops the horizontal slide? And the batter on deck isn''t really adding. Because he''s just standing stationary you don''t get a feeling that the play was at all close. As you continue with sports photography- look for one element to focus on. Maybe look to get the reaction from the guy on deck. IS he jumping around or what? Wait for the ump to call the play safe or out before snapping. You just need something else to pop this shot up a level. So was the guy safe or not? And if he was- was he playing for your team? :)</td>', 'I like the crop and the action. My biggest concern with this image would be the overall clutter in the shot. Nothing is really isolated out here. With the ump right on top of the play the motion is interrupted. See how he basically creates a vertical line that stops the horizontal slide? And the batter on deck isn''t really adding. Because he''s just standing stationary you don''t get a feeling that the play was at all close. As you continue with sports photography- look for one element to focus on. Maybe look to get the reaction from the guy on deck. IS he jumping around or what? Wait for the ump to call the play safe or out before snapping. You just need something else to pop this shot up a level. So was the guy safe or not? And if he was- was he playing for your team? :)', '2005-04-17 13:34:58.000000', NULL, 1),
(1297845, 165150, 7560, '<td valign="top">This week''s award for most daring use of the camera. Woo. I''m feeling a case of vertigo coming on...<br/> <br/>Straight down would be so cool.</td>', 'This week''s award for most daring use of the camera. Woo. I''m feeling a case of vertigo coming on... Straight down would be so cool.', '2005-04-17 13:38:15.000000', NULL, 1),
