(1301331, 165010, 15832, '<td valign="top">WOW... Thanks for great comments!!!<br/>I cant descripe how happy i´am!<br/>Thanks to my good friend Patrik and his 9 years experience to make this posssible!<br/>The tailwhip was just one of many tricks he did for me. He also did the No-footedcancan,Nothing,cowboy,canadian nosepick and more...<br/>I´m gonna put some of those photos in my portifolio in the next days when i´m home.<br/> <br/>Thanks again......<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2005-04-18 18:55:30.</i></td>', 'WOW... Thanks for great comments!!!I cant descripe how happy i´am!Thanks to my good friend Patrik and his 9 years experience to make this posssible!The tailwhip was just one of many tricks he did for me. He also did the No-footedcancan,Nothing,cowboy,canadian nosepick and more...I´m gonna put some of those photos in my portifolio in the next days when i´m home. Thanks again......', '2005-04-18 17:45:21.000000', '2005-04-18 19:55:30.000000', 0),
(1301338, 164797, 3569, '<td valign="top">I figured this was how ya did it.  I''ve shot so many cans and there are always dents all over the can when ya really shoot one.  Great placing and shot though.  Van</td>', 'I figured this was how ya did it.  I''ve shot so many cans and there are always dents all over the can when ya really shoot one.  Great placing and shot though.  Van', '2005-04-18 17:47:22.000000', NULL, 0),
(1301458, 165017, 6999, '<td valign="top">I''ve come to this through the 350D page - and I can''t believe it isn''t up near the top of that page. There are certainly elements I''d want to correct with another session - impact would be gained from a crop that placed the skater a touch more strongly, and keeping an entire shadow would have emphasised the disconnection from the ground - but your sense of the graphic in the background, the brightness and toning across those surfaces really speak of the bright sun - those should surely have got you a higher score ... neat work</td>', 'I''ve come to this through the 350D page - and I can''t believe it isn''t up near the top of that page. There are certainly elements I''d want to correct with another session - impact would be gained from a crop that placed the skater a touch more strongly, and keeping an entire shadow would have emphasised the disconnection from the ground - but your sense of the graphic in the background, the brightness and toning across those surfaces really speak of the bright sun - those should surely have got you a higher score ... neat work', '2005-04-18 18:33:23.000000', NULL, 0),
(1301484, 165064, 31875, '<td valign="top">Thanks so much for nice comments! My first ribbon! <br/> <br/>I used Canon 28-135 IS at 135mm and still had to make almost 100% crop. Too bad I didnt have yet a new 70-200 f4 which arrived just one day after I took this shoot.</td>', 'Thanks so much for nice comments! My first ribbon!  I used Canon 28-135 IS at 135mm and still had to make almost 100% crop. Too bad I didnt have yet a new 70-200 f4 which arrived just one day after I took this shoot.', '2005-04-18 18:43:37.000000', NULL, 0),
