(1307030, 165187, 93, '<td valign="top">This was YOURS!!!!  OMG.. it was my only 10 :)<br/> <br/>I should have recognized your style.</td>', 'This was YOURS!!!!  OMG.. it was my only 10 :) I should have recognized your style.', '2005-04-20 03:23:33.000000', NULL, 0),
(1307327, 165010, 9290, '<td valign="top">Extreme Sports Indeed! Well done.</td>', 'Extreme Sports Indeed! Well done.', '2005-04-20 08:05:38.000000', NULL, 0),
(1307809, 164900, 20315, '<td valign="top">I like this photo because it grabs me in a couple of different ways. <br/> <br/>At first glance it''s moody and very graphic but upon realizing the little fish eyes in the midst of the motion blur, it takes on a whimsical nature. The fish look like eels with their motion blur extensions. <br/> <br/>One thing I would like to see is more action at the top 2/3 of the frame and a concentration of fish eyes off center. I say this because although this photo has a lot of great movement, it is a bit static because the focus is at the bottom third of the frame and is front and center. <br/> <br/>Thumbs up for creativity and going outside the norm. <br/> <br/>Keep taking great shots!<br/> <br/>All the best,<br/> <br/>Christina Mallet<br/>(DP Critique Club)<br/></td>', 'I like this photo because it grabs me in a couple of different ways.  At first glance it''s moody and very graphic but upon realizing the little fish eyes in the midst of the motion blur, it takes on a whimsical nature. The fish look like eels with their motion blur extensions.  One thing I would like to see is more action at the top 2/3 of the frame and a concentration of fish eyes off center. I say this because although this photo has a lot of great movement, it is a bit static because the focus is at the bottom third of the frame and is front and center.  Thumbs up for creativity and going outside the norm.  Keep taking great shots! All the best, Christina Mallet(DP Critique Club)', '2005-04-20 12:18:52.000000', NULL, 0),
(1307851, 165048, 20315, '<td valign="top">Although this photo depicts action it feels somewhat static to me because of the front and center positioning of the subject and the angle for which the shot was taken. The movement of the skier could have been improved by capturing him either farther out in the frame or by cropping. <br/> <br/>If you had crouched a little lower you might have been able to get more height to the spray from his turn.<br/> <br/>Additionally, I think this photo would be more interesting if the primary subject were in the top 2/3 of the photo. There''s a bit too much sky and empty space in the photo which I find distracting. <br/> <br/>All the best, <br/> <br/>Christina Mallet<br/>(DP Critique Club)<br/> <br/></td>', 'Although this photo depicts action it feels somewhat static to me because of the front and center positioning of the subject and the angle for which the shot was taken. The movement of the skier could have been improved by capturing him either farther out in the frame or by cropping.  If you had crouched a little lower you might have been able to get more height to the spray from his turn. Additionally, I think this photo would be more interesting if the primary subject were in the top 2/3 of the photo. There''s a bit too much sky and empty space in the photo which I find distracting.  All the best,  Christina Mallet(DP Critique Club) ', '2005-04-20 12:31:22.000000', NULL, 0),
(1307881, 164271, 20315, '<td valign="top">I really like the way you captured this subject. Because it''s off center and seems to shoot from the bottom corner of the frame it keeps the viewers eyes moving and really conveys a sense of action. <br/> <br/>I think the colors are fantastic and I really like the motion blur of the ride. That said however, I''m not so crazy about the motion blur in the background because it makes all the motion blur makes it difficult to look at this photo for long because you start to feel like you just stepped off the ride. On the other hand, I think it''s great that your photo can produce this result, but aesthetically speaking it would be an even stronger image if you had used a tripod so that you didn''t have blur in the background. <br/> <br/>Oh, and for the record, it''s okay for you to call this place a fun fair. It''s true that people say carnival in the US but that doesn''t mean you have to. <br/> <br/>Keep up the creativity and shooting!<br/> <br/>All the best, <br/>Christina Mallet<br/>(DP Critique Club)<br/></td>', 'I really like the way you captured this subject. Because it''s off center and seems to shoot from the bottom corner of the frame it keeps the viewers eyes moving and really conveys a sense of action.  I think the colors are fantastic and I really like the motion blur of the ride. That said however, I''m not so crazy about the motion blur in the background because it makes all the motion blur makes it difficult to look at this photo for long because you start to feel like you just stepped off the ride. On the other hand, I think it''s great that your photo can produce this result, but aesthetically speaking it would be an even stronger image if you had used a tripod so that you didn''t have blur in the background.  Oh, and for the record, it''s okay for you to call this place a fun fair. It''s true that people say carnival in the US but that doesn''t mean you have to.  Keep up the creativity and shooting! All the best, Christina Mallet(DP Critique Club)', '2005-04-20 12:41:08.000000', NULL, 0),
